{"key":"nlp-basics-u3-01","seriesId":"nlp-basics","episode":"u3-01","title":"Constituency Parsing: Sentences as Trees","fps":30,"duration":218.389,"durationInFrames":6552,"video":{"width":1920,"height":1080,"burnCaptions":true,"brand":"learnvi.in"},"badge":["UNIT 3 · LESSON 1","CONSTITUENCY PARSING"],"series":{"title":"NLP, Simply Explained","subtitle":"University NLP, one idea at a time, no heavy maths","runningPrompt":"","stops":[{"id":"u1-01","number":1,"name":"The Stages of NLP: From Letters to Meaning","stamp":"THE STAGES OF NLP: FROM LETTERS TO MEANING","topic":""},{"id":"u1-02","number":2,"name":"Tokenization: How Text Becomes Pieces","stamp":"TOKENIZATION: HOW TEXT BECOMES PIECES","topic":""},{"id":"u1-03","number":3,"name":"Text Classification: Teaching Computers to Sort Text","stamp":"TEXT CLASSIFICATION: TEACHING COMPUTERS TO SORT TEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u1-04","number":4,"name":"Language Models: Guessing the Next Word","stamp":"LANGUAGE MODELS: GUESSING THE NEXT WORD","topic":""},{"id":"u2-01","number":5,"name":"Morphology: The Building Blocks Inside Words","stamp":"MORPHOLOGY: THE BUILDING BLOCKS INSIDE WORDS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-02","number":6,"name":"Part-of-Speech Tagging: Is It a Noun or a Verb?","stamp":"PART-OF-SPEECH TAGGING: IS IT A NOUN OR A VERB?","topic":""},{"id":"u2-03","number":7,"name":"Chunking: Grouping Words into Phrases","stamp":"CHUNKING: GROUPING WORDS INTO PHRASES","topic":""},{"id":"u2-04","number":8,"name":"Generative vs Discriminative Models","stamp":"GENERATIVE VS DISCRIMINATIVE MODELS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-05","number":9,"name":"Hidden Markov Models, Intuitively","stamp":"HIDDEN MARKOV MODELS, INTUITIVELY","topic":""},{"id":"u2-06","number":10,"name":"Conditional Random Fields, Intuitively","stamp":"CONDITIONAL RANDOM FIELDS, INTUITIVELY","topic":""},{"id":"u3-01","number":11,"name":"Constituency Parsing: Sentences as Trees","stamp":"CONSTITUENCY PARSING: SENTENCES AS TREES","topic":""},{"id":"u3-02","number":12,"name":"Dependency Parsing: Who Did What to Whom","stamp":"DEPENDENCY PARSING: WHO DID WHAT TO WHOM","topic":""},{"id":"u3-03","number":13,"name":"Transition-Based Parsing: Building Trees Step by Step","stamp":"TRANSITION-BASED PARSING: BUILDING TREES STEP BY STEP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-01","number":14,"name":"Word Vectors: Giving Words a Place on a Map","stamp":"WORD VECTORS: GIVING WORDS A PLACE ON A MAP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-02","number":15,"name":"Word2Vec: Learning Word Vectors from Context","stamp":"WORD2VEC: LEARNING WORD VECTORS FROM CONTEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u4-03","number":16,"name":"Recurrent Neural Networks: Reading with Memory","stamp":"RECURRENT NEURAL NETWORKS: READING WITH MEMORY","topic":""},{"id":"u4-04","number":17,"name":"LSTMs: Remembering What Matters","stamp":"LSTMS: REMEMBERING WHAT MATTERS","topic":""},{"id":"u5-01","number":18,"name":"Contextual Embeddings and ELMo","stamp":"CONTEXTUAL EMBEDDINGS AND ELMO","topic":""},{"id":"u5-02","number":19,"name":"BERT: Reading in Both Directions","stamp":"BERT: READING IN BOTH DIRECTIONS","topic":""}]},"stop":{"number":11,"name":"Constituency Parsing: Sentences as Trees","stamp":"CONSTITUENCY PARSING: SENTENCES AS TREES"},"shorts":{"width":1080,"height":1920,"maxSeconds":60,"cta":"Full lesson: NLP, Simply Explained · Unit 3"},"thumbnail":{"headline":"How AI sees a sentence as a tree","big":"S → NP VP"},"segments":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","component":"TitleCard","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c01","start":0.6,"end":6.943,"marks":{},"text":"Welcome to unit three of NLP, Simply Explained. This is lesson 1: constituency parsing.","words":[{"w":"Welcome","start":0.6},{"w":"to","start":1.04},{"w":"unit","start":1.24},{"w":"three","start":1.6},{"w":"of","start":1.96},{"w":"NLP,","start":2.32},{"w":"Simply","start":2.68},{"w":"Explained.","start":3.32},{"w":"This","start":4.12},{"w":"is","start":4.467},{"w":"lesson","start":4.813},{"w":"1:","start":5.16},{"w":"constituency","start":5.48},{"w":"parsing.","start":6.4}]},{"id":"c02","start":7.343,"end":15.32,"marks":{},"text":"In unit two we tagged words and grouped them into small chunks. Now we go all the way, and find the complete structure of a sentence.","words":[{"w":"In","start":7.343},{"w":"unit","start":7.503},{"w":"two","start":7.843},{"w":"we","start":8.183},{"w":"tagged","start":8.383},{"w":"words","start":8.783},{"w":"and","start":9.143},{"w":"grouped","start":9.343},{"w":"them","start":9.703},{"w":"into","start":9.903},{"w":"small","start":10.33},{"w":"chunks.","start":10.756},{"w":"Now","start":11.183},{"w":"we","start":11.543},{"w":"go","start":11.783},{"w":"all","start":12.063},{"w":"the","start":12.263},{"w":"way,","start":12.463},{"w":"and","start":12.743},{"w":"find","start":13.023},{"w":"the","start":13.303},{"w":"complete","start":13.463},{"w":"structure","start":13.983},{"w":"of","start":14.463},{"w":"a","start":14.583},{"w":"sentence.","start":14.703}]}],"title":"Welcome","shortTitle":"Welcome","props":{"kicker":"Unit 3 · Lesson 1","title":"Constituency Parsing","subtitle":"Sentences as trees"},"start":0.6,"end":15.32,"startFrame":0,"durationInFrames":487},{"id":"idea","kind":"core","component":"BigIdea","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c03","start":16.233,"end":23.363,"marks":{},"text":"Here's the idea. A sentence isn't a flat list of words. It's a tree: phrases nested inside bigger phrases.","words":[{"w":"Here's","start":16.233},{"w":"the","start":16.593},{"w":"idea.","start":16.793},{"w":"A","start":17.353},{"w":"sentence","start":17.593},{"w":"isn't","start":18.113},{"w":"a","start":18.433},{"w":"flat","start":18.553},{"w":"list","start":18.873},{"w":"of","start":19.113},{"w":"words.","start":19.273},{"w":"It's","start":19.753},{"w":"a","start":20.073},{"w":"tree:","start":20.233},{"w":"phrases","start":20.713},{"w":"nested","start":21.433},{"w":"inside","start":21.873},{"w":"bigger","start":22.313},{"w":"phrases.","start":22.713}]}],"title":"The big idea","shortTitle":"The big idea","props":{"kicker":"Key idea","text":"A sentence isn't a flat list of words. It's a tree of phrases inside phrases.","highlight":["tree"]},"start":16.233,"end":23.363,"startFrame":487,"durationInFrames":241},{"id":"constituent","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c04","start":24.267,"end":33.931,"marks":{},"text":"The building blocks are called constituents. A constituent is a group of words that works as one unit. A quick test: can you replace the group with a single word?","words":[{"w":"The","start":24.267},{"w":"building","start":24.387},{"w":"blocks","start":24.787},{"w":"are","start":25.187},{"w":"called","start":25.387},{"w":"constituents.","start":25.707},{"w":"A","start":26.707},{"w":"constituent","start":26.907},{"w":"is","start":27.707},{"w":"a","start":27.827},{"w":"group","start":27.947},{"w":"of","start":28.187},{"w":"words","start":28.347},{"w":"that","start":28.667},{"w":"works","start":28.867},{"w":"as","start":29.187},{"w":"one","start":29.387},{"w":"unit.","start":29.667},{"w":"A","start":29.947},{"w":"quick","start":30.227},{"w":"test:","start":30.867},{"w":"can","start":31.467},{"w":"you","start":31.707},{"w":"replace","start":31.867},{"w":"the","start":32.347},{"w":"group","start":32.507},{"w":"with","start":32.827},{"w":"a","start":32.947},{"w":"single","start":33.107},{"w":"word?","start":33.587}]},{"id":"c05","start":34.331,"end":40.198,"marks":{},"text":"In \"the old man slept\", you can replace \"the old man\" with \"he\". So \"the old man\" is a constituent.","words":[{"w":"In","start":34.331},{"w":"\"the","start":34.491},{"w":"old","start":34.651},{"w":"man","start":34.971},{"w":"slept\",","start":35.211},{"w":"you","start":35.771},{"w":"can","start":35.971},{"w":"replace","start":36.131},{"w":"\"the","start":36.571},{"w":"old","start":36.731},{"w":"man\"","start":37.051},{"w":"with","start":37.291},{"w":"\"he\".","start":37.531},{"w":"So","start":37.931},{"w":"\"the","start":38.211},{"w":"old","start":38.451},{"w":"man\"","start":38.731},{"w":"is","start":39.051},{"w":"a","start":39.251},{"w":"constituent.","start":39.371}]},{"id":"c06","start":40.598,"end":47.938,"marks":{},"text":"Think of nesting boxes. Small boxes are packed inside bigger boxes, and the biggest box holds the whole sentence.","words":[{"w":"Think","start":40.598},{"w":"of","start":40.798},{"w":"nesting","start":40.958},{"w":"boxes.","start":41.478},{"w":"Small","start":42.358},{"w":"boxes","start":42.718},{"w":"are","start":43.318},{"w":"packed","start":43.518},{"w":"inside","start":43.878},{"w":"bigger","start":44.278},{"w":"boxes,","start":44.678},{"w":"and","start":45.318},{"w":"the","start":45.478},{"w":"biggest","start":45.678},{"w":"box","start":46.158},{"w":"holds","start":46.518},{"w":"the","start":46.878},{"w":"whole","start":47.038},{"w":"sentence.","start":47.318}]}],"title":"What is a constituent?","shortTitle":"What is a constituent?","props":{"kicker":"Definition","term":"Constituent","definition":"A group of words that works as one unit in a sentence. Quick test: can you replace it with a single word?","example":"[the old man] slept → [he] slept","analogy":"Nesting boxes: small boxes packed inside bigger boxes."},"start":24.267,"end":47.938,"startFrame":728,"durationInFrames":738},{"id":"build","kind":"core","component":"Steps","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c07","start":48.867,"end":52.379,"marks":{},"text":"Let's build the tree for \"the old man slept\", from the bottom up.","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":48.867},{"w":"build","start":49.227},{"w":"the","start":49.467},{"w":"tree","start":49.627},{"w":"for","start":49.907},{"w":"\"the","start":50.067},{"w":"old","start":50.227},{"w":"man","start":50.507},{"w":"slept\",","start":50.747},{"w":"from","start":51.347},{"w":"the","start":51.507},{"w":"bottom","start":51.667},{"w":"up.","start":52.147}]},{"id":"c08","start":52.779,"end":55.921,"marks":{},"text":"Words: we start with the four words at the bottom of the tree.","words":[{"w":"Words:","start":52.779},{"w":"we","start":53.339},{"w":"start","start":53.539},{"w":"with","start":53.899},{"w":"the","start":54.019},{"w":"four","start":54.239},{"w":"words","start":54.459},{"w":"at","start":54.779},{"w":"the","start":54.899},{"w":"bottom","start":55.019},{"w":"of","start":55.379},{"w":"the","start":55.459},{"w":"tree.","start":55.619}]},{"id":"c09","start":56.321,"end":60.438,"marks":{},"text":"Noun phrase: \"the old man\" joins into one noun phrase, NP.","words":[{"w":"Noun","start":56.321},{"w":"phrase:","start":56.721},{"w":"\"the","start":57.281},{"w":"old","start":57.521},{"w":"man\"","start":57.801},{"w":"joins","start":58.161},{"w":"into","start":58.641},{"w":"one","start":58.841},{"w":"noun","start":59.081},{"w":"phrase,","start":59.361},{"w":"NP.","start":59.9}]},{"id":"c10","start":60.838,"end":63.995,"marks":{},"text":"Verb phrase: \"slept\" forms the verb phrase, VP.","words":[{"w":"Verb","start":60.878},{"w":"phrase:","start":61.318},{"w":"\"slept\"","start":61.758},{"w":"forms","start":62.198},{"w":"the","start":62.451},{"w":"verb","start":62.705},{"w":"phrase,","start":62.958},{"w":"VP.","start":63.477}]},{"id":"c11","start":64.395,"end":71.307,"marks":{},"text":"Sentence: finally, the noun phrase and the verb phrase join into the whole sentence, S, at the top of the tree.","words":[{"w":"Sentence:","start":64.395},{"w":"finally,","start":65.115},{"w":"the","start":65.915},{"w":"noun","start":66.155},{"w":"phrase","start":66.475},{"w":"and","start":66.875},{"w":"the","start":67.062},{"w":"verb","start":67.248},{"w":"phrase","start":67.435},{"w":"join","start":67.915},{"w":"into","start":68.235},{"w":"the","start":68.435},{"w":"whole","start":68.555},{"w":"sentence,","start":68.875},{"w":"S,","start":69.755},{"w":"at","start":69.995},{"w":"the","start":70.235},{"w":"top","start":70.395},{"w":"of","start":70.715},{"w":"the","start":70.795},{"w":"tree.","start":70.955}]}],"title":"Building a tree","shortTitle":"Building a tree","props":{"kicker":"Bottom up","title":"Building the tree for “the old man slept”","steps":[{"label":"Words","detail":"the · old · man · slept"},{"label":"Noun phrase","detail":"the old man → NP"},{"label":"Verb phrase","detail":"slept → VP"},{"label":"Sentence","detail":"NP + VP → S"}]},"start":48.867,"end":71.307,"startFrame":1466,"durationInFrames":701},{"id":"grammar","kind":"core","component":"Table","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c12","start":72.233,"end":78.716,"marks":{},"text":"A parser knows which joins are allowed from a set of rules, called a context-free grammar. Here's a tiny one.","words":[{"w":"A","start":72.233},{"w":"parser","start":72.313},{"w":"knows","start":72.793},{"w":"which","start":73.113},{"w":"joins","start":73.353},{"w":"are","start":73.753},{"w":"allowed","start":73.913},{"w":"from","start":74.273},{"w":"a","start":74.393},{"w":"set","start":74.513},{"w":"of","start":74.713},{"w":"rules,","start":74.873},{"w":"called","start":75.353},{"w":"a","start":75.713},{"w":"context-free","start":76.233},{"w":"grammar.","start":76.753},{"w":"Here's","start":77.353},{"w":"a","start":77.833},{"w":"tiny","start":77.993},{"w":"one.","start":78.433}]},{"id":"c13","start":79.116,"end":84.426,"marks":{},"text":"S goes to NP VP: a sentence is a noun phrase followed by a verb phrase.","words":[{"w":"S","start":79.396},{"w":"goes","start":79.676},{"w":"to","start":79.956},{"w":"NP","start":80.236},{"w":"VP:","start":80.516},{"w":"a","start":80.796},{"w":"sentence","start":81.156},{"w":"is","start":81.756},{"w":"a","start":81.916},{"w":"noun","start":82.076},{"w":"phrase","start":82.396},{"w":"followed","start":82.916},{"w":"by","start":83.356},{"w":"a","start":83.556},{"w":"verb","start":83.756},{"w":"phrase.","start":83.956}]},{"id":"c14","start":84.826,"end":88.827,"marks":{},"text":"NP goes to determiner, adjective, noun: like \"the old man\".","words":[{"w":"NP","start":85.046},{"w":"goes","start":85.266},{"w":"to","start":85.586},{"w":"determiner,","start":85.746},{"w":"adjective,","start":86.426},{"w":"noun:","start":87.146},{"w":"like","start":87.626},{"w":"\"the","start":87.906},{"w":"old","start":88.146},{"w":"man\".","start":88.466}]},{"id":"c15","start":89.227,"end":94.105,"marks":{},"text":"VP goes to VERB NP: a verb followed by its object, like \"saw a dog\".","words":[{"w":"VP","start":89.467},{"w":"goes","start":89.707},{"w":"to","start":90.067},{"w":"VERB","start":90.427},{"w":"NP:","start":90.787},{"w":"a","start":91.147},{"w":"verb","start":91.507},{"w":"followed","start":91.867},{"w":"by","start":92.187},{"w":"its","start":92.347},{"w":"object,","start":92.587},{"w":"like","start":93.107},{"w":"\"saw","start":93.347},{"w":"a","start":93.507},{"w":"dog\".","start":93.667}]},{"id":"c16","start":94.505,"end":97.957,"marks":{},"text":"And VP can also be just a verb on its own, like \"slept\".","words":[{"w":"And","start":94.718},{"w":"VP","start":94.932},{"w":"can","start":95.145},{"w":"also","start":95.385},{"w":"be","start":95.625},{"w":"just","start":95.785},{"w":"a","start":95.958},{"w":"verb","start":96.132},{"w":"on","start":96.305},{"w":"its","start":96.465},{"w":"own,","start":96.705},{"w":"like","start":97.065},{"w":"\"slept\".","start":97.385}]}],"title":"A tiny grammar","shortTitle":"A tiny grammar","props":{"kicker":"Context-free grammar","title":"A tiny grammar","columns":["Rule","Means","Example"],"rows":[["S → NP VP","noun phrase + verb phrase","the man | slept"],["NP → DET ADJ NOUN","the, a describing word, a noun","the old man"],["VP → VERB NP","a verb and its object","saw | a dog"],["VP → VERB","a verb on its own","slept"]],"highlight":[]},"start":72.233,"end":97.957,"startFrame":2167,"durationInFrames":799},{"id":"telescope","kind":"core","component":"Compare","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c17","start":98.867,"end":103.047,"marks":{},"text":"Here's why parsing is hard. Take: \"I saw the man with the telescope.\"","words":[{"w":"Here's","start":98.867},{"w":"why","start":99.187},{"w":"parsing","start":99.427},{"w":"is","start":99.907},{"w":"hard.","start":100.147},{"w":"Take:","start":100.627},{"w":"\"I","start":101.067},{"w":"saw","start":101.387},{"w":"the","start":101.587},{"w":"man","start":101.787},{"w":"with","start":102.027},{"w":"the","start":102.147},{"w":"telescope.\"","start":102.307}]},{"id":"c18","start":103.447,"end":109.146,"marks":{},"text":"In one tree, \"with the telescope\" belongs to \"the man\". The man is the one holding the telescope.","words":[{"w":"In","start":103.447},{"w":"one","start":103.647},{"w":"tree,","start":103.927},{"w":"\"with","start":104.407},{"w":"the","start":104.567},{"w":"telescope\"","start":104.727},{"w":"belongs","start":105.487},{"w":"to","start":105.967},{"w":"\"the","start":106.127},{"w":"man\".","start":106.287},{"w":"The","start":106.687},{"w":"man","start":106.967},{"w":"is","start":107.287},{"w":"the","start":107.487},{"w":"one","start":107.607},{"w":"holding","start":107.847},{"w":"the","start":108.247},{"w":"telescope.","start":108.407}]},{"id":"c19","start":109.546,"end":115.77,"marks":{},"text":"In the other tree, it belongs to \"saw\". I used the telescope to see him. Same words, two different trees.","words":[{"w":"In","start":109.546},{"w":"the","start":109.666},{"w":"other","start":109.786},{"w":"tree,","start":110.026},{"w":"it","start":110.346},{"w":"belongs","start":110.506},{"w":"to","start":110.946},{"w":"\"saw\".","start":111.146},{"w":"I","start":111.546},{"w":"used","start":111.846},{"w":"the","start":112.146},{"w":"telescope","start":112.266},{"w":"to","start":112.986},{"w":"see","start":113.146},{"w":"him.","start":113.426},{"w":"Same","start":113.826},{"w":"words,","start":114.186},{"w":"two","start":114.626},{"w":"different","start":114.866},{"w":"trees.","start":115.306}]}],"title":"One sentence, two trees","shortTitle":"One sentence, two meanings: the telescope problem","props":{"kicker":"Ambiguity","title":"“I saw the man with the telescope”","columns":[{"title":"Tree 1","items":["[saw] [the man with the telescope]","the man has the telescope"],"tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Tree 2","items":["[saw the man] [with the telescope]","I used the telescope"],"tone":"neutral"}],"verdict":{"text":"Same words, two different trees"}},"start":98.867,"end":115.77,"startFrame":2966,"durationInFrames":535},{"id":"pcfg","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c20","start":116.7,"end":133.758,"marks":{},"text":"So how does a parser choose between trees? It gives each grammar rule a probability. That's a probabilistic context-free grammar, or PCFG. The probabilities are learned by counting rules in a treebank: a large set of sentences that people have parsed by hand.","words":[{"w":"So","start":116.7},{"w":"how","start":116.86},{"w":"does","start":117.02},{"w":"a","start":117.18},{"w":"parser","start":117.3},{"w":"choose","start":117.74},{"w":"between","start":118.14},{"w":"trees?","start":118.46},{"w":"It","start":119.02},{"w":"gives","start":119.26},{"w":"each","start":119.58},{"w":"grammar","start":119.86},{"w":"rule","start":120.34},{"w":"a","start":120.62},{"w":"probability.","start":120.78},{"w":"That's","start":121.74},{"w":"a","start":122.14},{"w":"probabilistic","start":122.26},{"w":"context-free","start":123.12},{"w":"grammar,","start":123.98},{"w":"or","start":124.62},{"w":"PCFG.","start":125.5},{"w":"The","start":126.38},{"w":"probabilities","start":126.86},{"w":"are","start":127.74},{"w":"learned","start":127.98},{"w":"by","start":128.34},{"w":"counting","start":128.58},{"w":"rules","start":129.02},{"w":"in","start":129.38},{"w":"a","start":129.54},{"w":"treebank:","start":129.96},{"w":"a","start":130.38},{"w":"large","start":130.62},{"w":"set","start":130.98},{"w":"of","start":131.22},{"w":"sentences","start":131.34},{"w":"that","start":132.02},{"w":"people","start":132.22},{"w":"have","start":132.5},{"w":"parsed","start":132.7},{"w":"by","start":133.14},{"w":"hand.","start":133.38}]},{"id":"c21","start":134.158,"end":144.073,"marks":{},"text":"Common rules, like a verb followed by its object, get high probabilities. Rare rules get low ones. The tree whose rules are most likely overall wins.","words":[{"w":"Common","start":134.158},{"w":"rules,","start":134.558},{"w":"like","start":135.038},{"w":"a","start":135.291},{"w":"verb","start":135.545},{"w":"followed","start":135.798},{"w":"by","start":136.158},{"w":"its","start":136.318},{"w":"object,","start":136.558},{"w":"get","start":137.198},{"w":"high","start":137.478},{"w":"probabilities.","start":137.758},{"w":"Rare","start":138.958},{"w":"rules","start":139.398},{"w":"get","start":139.838},{"w":"low","start":140.078},{"w":"ones.","start":140.398},{"w":"The","start":140.798},{"w":"tree","start":141.038},{"w":"whose","start":141.358},{"w":"rules","start":141.678},{"w":"are","start":142.078},{"w":"most","start":142.278},{"w":"likely","start":142.558},{"w":"overall","start":143.063},{"w":"wins.","start":143.568}]},{"id":"c22","start":144.473,"end":149.696,"marks":{},"text":"Think of a sat-nav. There are many possible routes, and it picks the one most likely to get you there.","words":[{"w":"Think","start":144.473},{"w":"of","start":144.673},{"w":"a","start":144.793},{"w":"sat-nav.","start":145.233},{"w":"There","start":145.673},{"w":"are","start":145.873},{"w":"many","start":146.073},{"w":"possible","start":146.313},{"w":"routes,","start":146.873},{"w":"and","start":147.313},{"w":"it","start":147.473},{"w":"picks","start":147.633},{"w":"the","start":147.953},{"w":"one","start":148.073},{"w":"most","start":148.313},{"w":"likely","start":148.553},{"w":"to","start":148.873},{"w":"get","start":149.033},{"w":"you","start":149.233},{"w":"there.","start":149.433}]}],"title":"Choosing the likely tree","shortTitle":"Choosing the likely tree","props":{"kicker":"Probabilistic grammar","term":"PCFG","definition":"Probabilistic context-free grammar: each rule gets a probability, learned from a treebank, so the parser can pick the most likely tree.","example":"VP → VERB NP: common  ·  rare rules: unlikely","analogy":"A sat-nav picking the likeliest route among many roads."},"start":116.7,"end":149.696,"startFrame":3501,"durationInFrames":1017},{"id":"cky","kind":"core","component":"Bullets","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c23","start":150.6,"end":159.174,"marks":{},"text":"A sentence can have thousands of possible trees, so the parser needs a smart search. A classic one is called CKY. Here's the idea.","words":[{"w":"A","start":150.6},{"w":"sentence","start":150.72},{"w":"can","start":151.2},{"w":"have","start":151.4},{"w":"thousands","start":151.6},{"w":"of","start":152.08},{"w":"possible","start":152.24},{"w":"trees,","start":152.76},{"w":"so","start":153.24},{"w":"the","start":153.4},{"w":"parser","start":153.56},{"w":"needs","start":153.96},{"w":"a","start":154.28},{"w":"smart","start":154.44},{"w":"search.","start":154.84},{"w":"A","start":155.4},{"w":"classic","start":155.64},{"w":"one","start":156.2},{"w":"is","start":156.44},{"w":"called","start":156.6},{"w":"CKY.","start":157.24},{"w":"Here's","start":157.88},{"w":"the","start":158.44},{"w":"idea.","start":158.6}]},{"id":"c24","start":159.574,"end":163.124,"marks":{},"text":"First, find the best phrases for every pair of neighbouring words.","words":[{"w":"First,","start":159.574},{"w":"find","start":160.014},{"w":"the","start":160.334},{"w":"best","start":160.454},{"w":"phrases","start":160.694},{"w":"for","start":161.294},{"w":"every","start":161.494},{"w":"pair","start":161.734},{"w":"of","start":161.974},{"w":"neighbouring","start":162.134},{"w":"words.","start":162.734}]},{"id":"c25","start":163.524,"end":166.763,"marks":{},"text":"Then for every run of three words, then four, and so on.","words":[{"w":"Then","start":163.524},{"w":"for","start":163.724},{"w":"every","start":163.884},{"w":"run","start":164.164},{"w":"of","start":164.404},{"w":"three","start":164.604},{"w":"words,","start":164.884},{"w":"then","start":165.364},{"w":"four,","start":165.604},{"w":"and","start":165.924},{"w":"so","start":166.164},{"w":"on.","start":166.444}]},{"id":"c26","start":167.163,"end":172.641,"marks":{},"text":"Each bigger step reuses the small results already found, so nothing is worked out twice.","words":[{"w":"Each","start":167.163},{"w":"bigger","start":167.443},{"w":"step","start":167.803},{"w":"reuses","start":168.163},{"w":"the","start":168.763},{"w":"small","start":168.923},{"w":"results","start":169.243},{"w":"already","start":169.763},{"w":"found,","start":170.283},{"w":"so","start":170.683},{"w":"nothing","start":170.963},{"w":"is","start":171.323},{"w":"worked","start":171.563},{"w":"out","start":171.883},{"w":"twice.","start":172.123}]},{"id":"c27","start":173.041,"end":177.051,"marks":{},"text":"When it reaches the full sentence, the best tree over all the words wins.","words":[{"w":"When","start":173.041},{"w":"it","start":173.161},{"w":"reaches","start":173.281},{"w":"the","start":173.721},{"w":"full","start":173.841},{"w":"sentence,","start":174.121},{"w":"the","start":174.681},{"w":"best","start":174.921},{"w":"tree","start":175.281},{"w":"over","start":175.601},{"w":"all","start":175.841},{"w":"the","start":176.041},{"w":"words","start":176.201},{"w":"wins.","start":176.561}]}],"title":"How the search works","shortTitle":"How the search works","props":{"kicker":"The CKY idea","title":"How a parser searches for the best tree","items":[{"text":"Find the best phrases for every pair of words"},{"text":"Then for every run of three, four, and more"},{"text":"Reuse small results to build bigger ones"},{"text":"The best tree over the whole sentence wins"}],"numbered":false},"start":150.6,"end":177.051,"startFrame":4518,"durationInFrames":821},{"id":"quiz","kind":"quiz","component":"Quiz","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c28","start":177.967,"end":182.453,"marks":{},"text":"Quick quiz. Why does \"I saw the man with the telescope\" have two different trees?","words":[{"w":"Quick","start":178.234},{"w":"quiz.","start":178.5},{"w":"Why","start":178.767},{"w":"does","start":179.007},{"w":"\"I","start":179.247},{"w":"saw","start":179.447},{"w":"the","start":179.647},{"w":"man","start":179.807},{"w":"with","start":180.007},{"w":"the","start":180.127},{"w":"telescope\"","start":180.247},{"w":"have","start":181.087},{"w":"two","start":181.287},{"w":"different","start":181.487},{"w":"trees?","start":181.967}]},{"id":"c29","start":182.853,"end":184.373,"marks":{},"text":"Pause the video and choose.","words":[{"w":"Pause","start":182.853},{"w":"the","start":183.133},{"w":"video","start":183.393},{"w":"and","start":183.653},{"w":"choose.","start":183.853}]},{"id":"c30","start":187.773,"end":194.559,"marks":{},"text":"Because \"with the telescope\" can attach to \"saw\", or to \"the man\". Each choice gives a different tree, and a different meaning.","words":[{"w":"Because","start":187.773},{"w":"\"with","start":188.053},{"w":"the","start":188.253},{"w":"telescope\"","start":188.373},{"w":"can","start":189.053},{"w":"attach","start":189.213},{"w":"to","start":189.613},{"w":"\"saw\",","start":189.813},{"w":"or","start":190.253},{"w":"to","start":190.533},{"w":"\"the","start":190.693},{"w":"man\".","start":190.893},{"w":"Each","start":191.453},{"w":"choice","start":191.893},{"w":"gives","start":192.333},{"w":"a","start":192.613},{"w":"different","start":192.733},{"w":"tree,","start":193.093},{"w":"and","start":193.413},{"w":"a","start":193.613},{"w":"different","start":193.733},{"w":"meaning.","start":194.133}]}],"title":"Quick quiz","shortTitle":"Quick quiz: why two trees?","props":{"kicker":"Pause and predict","question":"Why does “I saw the man with the telescope” have two trees?","options":["Some words are misspelled","“with the telescope” can attach to “saw” or to “the man”","It has two verbs"],"answer":1,"explain":"The phrase can hang from either place in the tree, giving two meanings."},"start":177.967,"end":194.559,"startFrame":5339,"durationInFrames":525},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","component":"Recap","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c31","start":195.467,"end":199.559,"marks":{},"text":"Let's recap. A sentence is a tree of phrases inside phrases.","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":195.467},{"w":"recap.","start":195.827},{"w":"A","start":196.467},{"w":"sentence","start":196.667},{"w":"is","start":197.187},{"w":"a","start":197.347},{"w":"tree","start":197.467},{"w":"of","start":197.707},{"w":"phrases","start":197.867},{"w":"inside","start":198.387},{"w":"phrases.","start":198.867}]},{"id":"c32","start":199.959,"end":202.91,"marks":{},"text":"A context-free grammar lists which joins are allowed.","words":[{"w":"A","start":199.959},{"w":"context-free","start":200.419},{"w":"grammar","start":200.879},{"w":"lists","start":201.319},{"w":"which","start":201.639},{"w":"joins","start":201.879},{"w":"are","start":202.279},{"w":"allowed.","start":202.439}]},{"id":"c33","start":203.31,"end":206.467,"marks":{},"text":"Many sentences can be parsed into more than one tree.","words":[{"w":"Many","start":203.31},{"w":"sentences","start":203.67},{"w":"can","start":204.51},{"w":"be","start":204.67},{"w":"parsed","start":204.83},{"w":"into","start":205.23},{"w":"more","start":205.47},{"w":"than","start":205.71},{"w":"one","start":205.87},{"w":"tree.","start":206.11}]},{"id":"c34","start":206.867,"end":211.365,"marks":{},"text":"And a probabilistic grammar, a PCFG, picks the most likely tree.","words":[{"w":"And","start":206.867},{"w":"a","start":206.987},{"w":"probabilistic","start":207.107},{"w":"grammar,","start":207.907},{"w":"a","start":208.387},{"w":"PCFG,","start":208.812},{"w":"picks","start":209.238},{"w":"the","start":209.663},{"w":"most","start":210.089},{"w":"likely","start":210.514},{"w":"tree.","start":210.94}]},{"id":"c35","start":211.765,"end":216.889,"marks":{},"text":"Next lesson: Dependency Parsing. How do words in a sentence depend on each other?","words":[{"w":"Next","start":212.085},{"w":"lesson:","start":212.405},{"w":"Dependency","start":212.725},{"w":"Parsing.","start":213.605},{"w":"How","start":214.325},{"w":"do","start":214.605},{"w":"words","start":214.885},{"w":"in","start":215.165},{"w":"a","start":215.285},{"w":"sentence","start":215.405},{"w":"depend","start":215.845},{"w":"on","start":216.205},{"w":"each","start":216.365},{"w":"other?","start":216.605}]}],"title":"Recap and next lesson","shortTitle":"Recap and next lesson","props":{"title":"Recap","points":["Sentences are trees of phrases inside phrases","A context-free grammar says which joins are allowed","One sentence can have several trees","A PCFG picks the most likely tree"],"next":{"title":"Dependency Parsing","question":"How do words in a sentence depend on each other?"}},"start":195.467,"end":216.889,"startFrame":5864,"durationInFrames":688}],"refs":{"c01":0.6,"c02":7.343,"c03":16.233,"c04":24.267,"c05":34.331,"c06":40.598,"c07":48.867,"c08":52.779,"c09":56.321,"c10":60.838,"c11":64.395,"c12":72.233,"c13":79.116,"c14":84.826,"c15":89.227,"c16":94.505,"c17":98.867,"c18":103.447,"c19":109.546,"c20":116.7,"c21":134.158,"c22":144.473,"c23":150.6,"c24":159.574,"c25":163.524,"c26":167.163,"c27":173.041,"c28":177.967,"c29":182.853,"c30":187.773,"c31":195.467,"c32":199.959,"c33":203.31,"c34":206.867,"c35":211.765},"audio":[{"file":".cache/proc/7077416e2775e257.wav","start":0.6},{"file":".cache/proc/a73c11ed80c43d1e.wav","start":7.343},{"file":".cache/proc/65eb289f47b83cd6.wav","start":16.233},{"file":".cache/proc/6e2ae112cbe03ddb.wav","start":24.267},{"file":".cache/proc/6c698900ef3f4ec6.wav","start":34.331},{"file":".cache/proc/861a5482bffcb7c9.wav","start":40.598},{"file":".cache/proc/60f865c0cf9f6f99.wav","start":48.867},{"file":".cache/proc/7cd28183fc404de9.wav","start":52.779},{"file":".cache/proc/0dd88eea2219dab0.wav","start":56.321},{"file":".cache/proc/9221f537fe28ef25.wav","start":60.838},{"file":".cache/proc/cde8b061d9447da6.wav","start":64.395},{"file":".cache/proc/10d149cc1bd09dc4.wav","start":72.233},{"file":".cache/proc/26ec2dfce65481be.wav","start":79.116